Package: scNovoMOSim
Title: Simulate Single-Cell Multiome Data with Condition- and Cell-Type-Specific Gene Regulatory Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given ="Roxana Andreea", family ="Moldovan", email = "roxana.andreea.moldovan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6822-0224")),
    person(given ="Ana", family ="Conesa", role = "aut"),
    person(given ="Sonia", family ="Tarazona", role = "aut"))
Description: Simulates paired scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq count matrices with
    an explicit ground-truth gene regulatory network (GRN). The simulator
    supports multiple cell types and conditions, condition-specific GRN
    rewiring (edge addition, deletion, sign-flip and weight drift), and
    chromatin-accessibility-mediated transcriptional regulation. It is
    primarily intended for benchmarking GRN inference and differential
    network analysis tools for single-cell multiomics data.
